    "created_at": "2025-01-31T04:01:53Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-01-31T04:05:02Z",
    "body": "Hi @domenic,\n\n> We have to loosen up HTML to allow DOMString? enumerated attribute reflection that is not limited to only known values. This ends up looking like some version of 1 or 2, i.e., we have to decide the scope of this change and what precedent it sets.\n\nAfter discussion with @annevk @cookiecrook, and also with the ARIA WG (https://github.com/w3c/aria/issues/2414#issuecomment-2625714514), there is agreement that this approach you mentioned of relaxing the `DOMString?` getter to permit string reflection would meet ARIA's needs. I've submitted a PR with the proposed HTML spec change and would greatly appreciate your feedback. I would also note that this change is one of several proposed updates by the ARIA WG towards improving ARIA IDL to better align with HTML's reflection model and enumerated attribute behavior.  \n\nThank you!\n\nCC @annevk @cookiecrook @jnurthen @spectranaut\n\n",
